    "narrative": "Our offensive focus for today, August 10, centers on a trio of outfielders providing both floor and ceiling against favorable matchups. **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) leads the charge, benefiting from a high-utility spot in the lineup against Peralta; his +13% dynamic platoon edge and favorable park factors make him our premier start. **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65) is our most efficient table-setter, leveraging a +17% SP skill advantage and a wind-assisted park to warrant his leadoff positioning. Meanwhile, **Bryce Harper** (61.71) remains an auto-start in the utility slot; while Dobbins is a standard-issue arm, **Bryce Harper**\u2019s elite xwOBA metrics allow him to transcend the minor park-factor penalty, locking him into a high-tier scoring outcome.\n\nThe decision to bench **Gavin Sheets** (38.33) was the most difficult pivot on the slate. Despite a +7% dynamic platoon advantage, his projection was severely dampened by a -19% penalty against Henderson\u2019s elite profile. With the 40.0 floor threshold in place, **Gavin Sheets** failed to provide the necessary upside to displace our middle-tier starters like **Masyn Winn** (54.61) or **Justin Crawford** (54.72). We continue to monitor the status of **Will Smith**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Tyler Freeman**, who remain unavailable due to injury or scheduling, further tightening our flexibility.\n\nRisk mitigation remains a priority as we navigate today\u2019s matchups. **Jonathan Aranda** (65.13) carries a strong projection despite his disadvantageous L/L platoon against Lopez, buoyed heavily by the park and his #2 order spot. We are also keeping a close watch on **Daulton Varsho** (58.95), whose score is propped up by a wind-out forecast; should those conditions shift, his value could dip toward our marginal threshold. With no other major weather risks flagged, we are positioned to maximize our daily game caps by relying on the aggressive profiles of **Lawrence Butler** and **Jung Hoo Lee** to carry the offensive load against their respective right-handed opponents.",
